Lance Vesper is a tall, lanky human who looks far older than he is: pale, with deep bags under rheumy eyes, and an air of long illness. He wears a [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]] uniform four sizes too large for him, taken from someone far bulkier, and several belts hung with utility pouches.

He is in his mid-twenties, alive and human, and denies being a lich. What ailed him was a curse laid on him by a coven of nighthags, whom he angered in a swamp years ago, when he was younger and more arrogant. They drained his life to feed their own, so that he held a quarter of the span he should have and looked it. He had perhaps five or six years left, and no doctor could lift it. He is an overseer of the Scale, one of the troop under [[Org/The Scale/People/Ralph Bishop|Bishop]], and he hears the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]].

[[People/Argyle|Argyle]] broke the curse at last, after eight hours of ritual. Lance came out of it unchanged in body, but the cloud lifted from his face, his eyes grew less dark, and he stood a little straighter. He offered Argyle his gun in thanks, and when that was refused, a pin from his uniform: the Scale's symbol with his order's crest, which he said would tell his father that Argyle had helped him. His father is [[Org/The Scale/People/Macarius Vesper|Macarius Vesper]], second in command of the Scale.

He is one of Bishop's troop, and stood with him against the [[Bestiary/Void|void-thing]] that came through the tear over the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s dance floor.
